01:24:09.770 --> 01:24:12.677
And so the critics such as (indistinct),

01:24:17.290 --> 01:24:19.840
try to deal with the memories.

01:24:19.840 --> 01:24:23.280
Very important I think there the concept

01:24:23.280 --> 01:24:27.260
of our human experiences in history

01:24:27.260 --> 01:24:30.570
that we tend to forget, but don't forget.

01:24:30.570 --> 01:24:33.290
And that creates more
the psychological, again,

01:24:33.290 --> 01:24:37.110
the twist in the development
of the new world.

01:24:37.110 --> 01:24:39.880
But if you look at the works,

01:24:39.880 --> 01:24:42.660
literally works that you
can find lots of them

01:24:42.660 --> 01:24:47.660
as an important topics in
(indistinct) and then all these,

01:24:48.010 --> 01:24:50.980
that (indistinct) who experienced

01:24:52.115 --> 01:24:55.907
the logical distractions
and I myself, you know,

01:24:55.907 --> 01:24:59.430
was born and lived in Japan as a child,

01:24:59.430 --> 01:25:04.370
but I can't find any
remnant of my childhood life

01:25:04.370 --> 01:25:08.753
after the war because the
destruction was so complete.

01:25:09.840 --> 01:25:13.330
And so the airways just, you know,

01:25:13.330 --> 01:25:16.740
let everything disappear in one night,

01:25:16.740 --> 01:25:20.129
but the memory ring us
and what is very important

01:25:20.129 --> 01:25:23.600
is the memories, how we keep the memories,

01:25:23.600 --> 01:25:28.600
how we make a new hope
and then development

01:25:28.910 --> 01:25:33.880
out of digesting these memories
and not forgetting about it.

01:25:33.880 --> 01:25:36.150
And I think these other coaches' work

01:25:36.150 --> 01:25:38.750
was very in influential I think,

01:25:38.750 --> 01:25:43.750
that was written in late 1960s
in the (indistinct) period

01:25:44.290 --> 01:25:49.290
and this black market also
is a very interesting topics,

01:25:49.610 --> 01:25:54.610
I think, it developed into
the golden eye of (indistinct)

01:25:55.620 --> 01:25:58.103
and all these special, you know,

01:26:00.640 --> 01:26:05.640
the sections of Zakaya and
so forth came out of the

01:26:08.060 --> 01:26:13.060
black market areas and also
it's the area where foreigners,

01:26:13.250 --> 01:26:18.070
people who came back
from the colonial Korea

01:26:18.070 --> 01:26:23.070
and so forth, came there and
then had their own business

01:26:23.160 --> 01:26:27.177
that developed into the big
business of (indistinct)

01:26:27.177 --> 01:26:32.177
and then others and in the
development of the economics

01:26:33.660 --> 01:26:35.700
prosperity in Japan.

01:26:35.700 --> 01:26:39.580
So it is very new,

01:26:39.580 --> 01:26:44.143
but refreshing way of talking
about the post war phenomena

01:26:45.120 --> 01:26:47.880
and culture, not just always talking about

01:26:49.263 --> 01:26:51.250
the political issues of the government,

01:26:51.250 --> 01:26:54.940
criticizing how the
government had a long policy

01:26:54.940 --> 01:26:57.473
and so forth, but look at the topos

01:26:59.450 --> 01:27:02.163
that we built our post war life.

01:27:17.230 --> 01:27:19.010
- [Chloe] Thank you very much, Chloe Star.

01:27:19.010 --> 01:27:21.110
Do you think your women writers,

01:27:21.110 --> 01:27:25.340
reformulations of female
sexuality had any effect on

01:27:25.340 --> 01:27:28.970
male writers or men more
generally in their understanding

01:27:28.970 --> 01:27:31.983
of women's sexuality in the
period following the writing?

01:27:33.497 --> 01:27:35.050
- Right now in Japan?

01:27:35.050 --> 01:27:38.160
- [Chloe] I mean, in the decade
or two following, you know,

01:27:38.160 --> 01:27:41.980
the rethinking on women as not
necessarily just childbearing

01:27:41.980 --> 01:27:42.813
for example.

01:27:42.813 --> 01:27:43.977
- Oh, I see, yes.

01:27:43.977 --> 01:27:47.180
In the post war period in
Japan, it is very peculiar

01:27:48.490 --> 01:27:51.460
I think, abnormal in a sense that

01:27:53.540 --> 01:27:58.540
this discussion about the
society and the history

01:27:58.890 --> 01:28:03.280
are completely limited to
male thinkers and critics

01:28:03.280 --> 01:28:06.360
that putting all the experiences of women

01:28:06.360 --> 01:28:09.410
and also what women thought and expressed

01:28:09.410 --> 01:28:13.730
into a big parenthesis
that it is women's issues.

01:28:13.730 --> 01:28:18.070
And then it's the discuss
on feminist criticism

01:28:18.070 --> 01:28:22.513
and analysis, and that did not
exist, I think in the world,

01:28:23.360 --> 01:28:27.550
like since 1960s, France
has been dealing with these

01:28:27.550 --> 01:28:31.210
feminist issues and then the sexual norms,

01:28:31.210 --> 01:28:35.910
and then so forth very much
into the discussion integrated

01:28:35.910 --> 01:28:39.080
part of the thinking of the new world,

01:28:39.080 --> 01:28:42.803
but Japan somehow completing ignored.

01:28:43.760 --> 01:28:46.330
I think it is a question of the criticism,

01:28:46.330 --> 01:28:48.860
the critics in Japan,

01:28:48.860 --> 01:28:52.570
that they really thought
they can get away with

01:28:52.570 --> 01:28:56.220
facing these issues and then questions.

01:28:56.220 --> 01:28:58.350
And I think it would
have been very different.

01:28:58.350 --> 01:29:02.420
And also talking about female

01:29:02.420 --> 01:29:05.410
expressions, representations too,

01:29:05.410 --> 01:29:09.210
I think we have a different
images of post war period.

01:29:09.210 --> 01:29:13.470
And I think we could have
imagined differently much earlier

01:29:13.470 --> 01:29:16.920
if we talked about female experiences,

01:29:16.920 --> 01:29:21.920
how they accepted and
tried to transcend this

01:29:24.350 --> 01:29:28.740
really very agonizing
experience of new women,

01:29:28.740 --> 01:29:31.890
the phenomena of (indistinct) period

01:29:31.890 --> 01:29:36.890
and how the female body was controlled

01:29:37.250 --> 01:29:42.060
by the political, you know,
the policies during the war

01:29:42.060 --> 01:29:43.000
and so forth.

01:29:43.000 --> 01:29:47.020
We should have discussed material
and faced those questions,

01:29:47.020 --> 01:29:47.853
I think.

01:30:01.650 --> 01:30:02.993
- I had two questions.

01:30:04.037 --> 01:30:06.760
One, is really a clarification.

01:30:06.760 --> 01:30:10.110
I wondered, so am I correct in thinking

01:30:10.110 --> 01:30:15.110
that you were presenting
(indistinct) as a critique

01:30:15.780 --> 01:30:20.307
of the (indistinct)
position on (indistinct)?

01:30:21.770 --> 01:30:24.380
So rather than trying
to fix the (indistinct)

01:30:24.380 --> 01:30:28.510
we should accept it and
see what comes out of that.

01:30:28.510 --> 01:30:29.830
Is that the correct way to think about it?

01:30:29.830 --> 01:30:32.803
- Well, very it's very
much the post discourse.

01:30:34.500 --> 01:30:39.500
It's based on how to accept the
United States, it's policies

01:30:39.680 --> 01:30:43.580
and then in forming democratic nations

01:30:43.580 --> 01:30:46.780
with this peace constitution and so forth,

01:30:46.780 --> 01:30:50.910
it's divided in a radical
way that probably like doing

01:30:50.910 --> 01:30:55.890
people deject dependency on
the United States in America.

01:30:55.890 --> 01:31:00.590
And then others think that
despite the fact that,

01:31:00.590 --> 01:31:04.460
that we do did experience
and occupation areas,

01:31:04.460 --> 01:31:08.790
which was very much
controlled by the censorship,

01:31:08.790 --> 01:31:12.050
nevertheless, it was
a good thing for Japan

01:31:13.384 --> 01:31:17.530
that it came out of this
military control Imperial

01:31:18.403 --> 01:31:21.980
at the power into a new possibilities

01:31:21.980 --> 01:31:24.040
of the democratic develop.

01:31:24.040 --> 01:31:25.820
It's very much divided.

01:31:25.820 --> 01:31:28.670
But when you look at
the phenomenon through

01:31:28.670 --> 01:31:33.110
the women's perspective, the
things look very different.

01:31:33.110 --> 01:31:38.110
I mean, the existence of
America became, I mean,

01:31:38.440 --> 01:31:43.440
symbolically and not just
the outsiders or insider,

01:31:44.440 --> 01:31:49.440
but it became very complicated
part of the post war Japan

01:31:50.077 --> 01:31:53.423
development and it's
also have a sexual too,

01:31:54.780 --> 01:31:57.440
in a way that (indistinct) present

01:31:58.510 --> 01:32:03.510
that the boy who was born is
taken care of by a daughter

01:32:05.090 --> 01:32:10.090
who was born of American,
probably the soldiers or whatever.

01:32:13.290 --> 01:32:18.000
And then as a symbol
of atomic bomb damage,

01:32:18.000 --> 01:32:22.710
but then has to be really
accepted and then to have a new

01:32:22.710 --> 01:32:27.270
baby out of the symbol
of the atomic weapon,

01:32:27.270 --> 01:32:31.283
that's the only start of our overcoming,

01:32:32.400 --> 01:32:36.770
this (indistinct) post war phenomenon.

01:32:36.770 --> 01:32:40.290
So she's positive at the
same time, very critical

01:32:40.290 --> 01:32:45.120
and rejecting this discourse
developed by made critics,

01:32:45.120 --> 01:32:46.273
I think in general.

01:32:48.690 --> 01:32:50.120
- Thank you.

01:32:50.120 --> 01:32:53.680
The second question if I may is,

01:32:53.680 --> 01:32:56.910
so you spoke a lot about
the need to overcome

01:32:56.910 --> 01:33:00.080
the question of atomic
war and atomic weapons.

01:33:00.080 --> 01:33:03.150
And I wondered not to
speak on behalf of people

01:33:03.150 --> 01:33:03.983
who are younger,

01:33:03.983 --> 01:33:08.070
but my sense today is that
the question of climate change

01:33:08.070 --> 01:33:11.880
and the anthropocene has
somehow dwarfed the question

01:33:11.880 --> 01:33:13.510
of nuclear war.

01:33:13.510 --> 01:33:16.980
So the nuclear question has now become one

01:33:16.980 --> 01:33:20.710
that is a kind of subset
of this bigger problem,

01:33:20.710 --> 01:33:23.490
both of which basically
spelled the possibility

01:33:23.490 --> 01:33:26.353
of the end of the world as we know it.

01:33:27.620 --> 01:33:30.970
But I wonder how you think
about that problem and those two

01:33:30.970 --> 01:33:34.670
things in relation to each
other, particularly given that,

01:33:34.670 --> 01:33:37.440
whereas Japan has had
the unique experience of

01:33:39.520 --> 01:33:43.063
being bombed by atomic weapons,

01:33:44.000 --> 01:33:45.620
the question of climate change,

01:33:45.620 --> 01:33:48.310
and this bigger question of
the destruction of the world

01:33:48.310 --> 01:33:52.090
is one that really is universal
in a very different way.

01:33:52.090 --> 01:33:54.380
So I wonder if you have
any thoughts about those?

01:33:54.380 --> 01:33:57.880
- Well, I think that my
experiences in the United States,

01:33:57.880 --> 01:34:02.880
in 1960s is that I was
really struck by the fact

01:34:03.400 --> 01:34:08.400
most of the American justifies
the use of the atomic bomb,

01:34:08.640 --> 01:34:13.510
that it is a method to end the war,

01:34:13.510 --> 01:34:17.863
and also even to save Japanese
from a mass (indistinct).

01:34:20.740 --> 01:34:25.610
And it was a unbelievable
for those who witnessed

01:34:25.610 --> 01:34:28.560
the real damage of the nuclear weapon.

01:34:28.560 --> 01:34:33.560
It's really very brutal and
unbelievably, just, you know,

01:34:35.550 --> 01:34:39.370
unbelievable agony was
put to human beings.

01:34:39.370 --> 01:34:42.740
And also it's very much
related to the, you know,

01:34:42.740 --> 01:34:44.330
the parts of the children.

01:34:44.330 --> 01:34:47.820
We know the effect of
the radio activities.

01:34:47.820 --> 01:34:52.803
It's very serious for our, you know,

01:34:54.571 --> 01:34:57.010
the futility and the strategy,
and then so and so forth.

01:34:57.010 --> 01:35:01.653
And it also stays on in
the earth in the water,

01:35:03.503 --> 01:35:06.320
and circulate to damage the earth.

01:35:06.320 --> 01:35:09.120
It is one of the most serious,

01:35:09.120 --> 01:35:13.840
you know, experiences we
had during the war, I think,

01:35:13.840 --> 01:35:16.730
but to look at the world right now,

01:35:16.730 --> 01:35:21.730
no one is seriously
discussing the control of

01:35:23.270 --> 01:35:25.500
the atomic weapon and so forth.

01:35:25.500 --> 01:35:29.070
But I think from the
environmental standpoint of view,

01:35:29.070 --> 01:35:32.050
I think younger generation
will come to understand

01:35:32.050 --> 01:35:37.050
that if you use the nuclear power,

01:35:40.970 --> 01:35:43.823
you will have to deal
with the tremendous waste.

01:35:45.430 --> 01:35:50.430
And it's a gummy garbage
that not only the earth

01:35:50.530 --> 01:35:54.210
but the universe has to deal with.

01:35:54.210 --> 01:35:57.920
And it is such a most uneconomical

01:35:58.940 --> 01:36:03.320
and futuristic attempt
to use the electricity

01:36:03.320 --> 01:36:06.080
for the immediate purpose of development.

01:36:06.080 --> 01:36:09.620
People say we need it, the electricity.

01:36:09.620 --> 01:36:14.620
It's very essential, but to
use even the nuclear reactor.

01:36:15.280 --> 01:36:19.740
And then of course we face
the danger of Ukrainian.

01:36:19.740 --> 01:36:20.890
You know, the conflict,

01:36:22.160 --> 01:36:26.400
even though the nuclear
reactor is not used,

01:36:26.400 --> 01:36:27.723
still it is bombed.

01:36:28.660 --> 01:36:30.550
Then all the radioactivities will come out

01:36:30.550 --> 01:36:34.763
and then damage the
earth almost permanently.

01:36:35.930 --> 01:36:40.520
And that is a kind of the
heritage that the second world war

01:36:41.620 --> 01:36:44.563
left to us and we have
to face it, I think.

01:36:46.500 --> 01:36:50.410
I very strongly believe
that this kind of waste

01:36:50.410 --> 01:36:55.380
that the human development
or happiness or whatever,

01:36:55.380 --> 01:36:57.650
the convenience and so forth,

01:36:57.650 --> 01:37:02.370
it's really the boomerang
that will come back to us

01:37:02.370 --> 01:37:04.553
and then we have to do something about it.

01:37:08.915 --> 01:37:09.915
- Thank you.

01:37:14.222 --> 01:37:19.222
- Thank you so much
everybody (indistinct).

01:37:20.996 --> 01:37:24.079
And thank Professor Mizuta (indistinct).

01:37:24.079 --> 01:37:26.675
